{"id": "NOANS-008", "question": "Ngày cụ thể Leave Policy chính thức có hiệu lực là khi nào?", "tenant": "default", "expect_refusal": true, "reason": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "expected_sources": ["leave_policy"], "forbidden_source_ids": [], "probe_terms": ["hiệu lực", "effective"], "forbidden_detail": "exact_effective_date", "notes": "ADVERSARIAL PARTIAL EVIDENCE. The corpus states the policy EXISTS and carries a 'Hiệu lực' metadata field dated 01/01/2024 in its header table, but that header is document metadata, not a policy clause, and the retrieval chunks that answer annual-leave questions do not carry it. Scoring the answer as authorized on the strength of the header would be inferring a clause the document never states as policy. This is the case that separates a real abstention gate from a topical-similarity gate."}
